  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The derivative is the instantaneous rate of change: the slope of the tangent line, defined as a limit of average rates.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Below, \\( f(x)=\\tfrac{x^{3}}{3}-x \\) is in indigo and its derivative \\( f'(x)=x^{2}-1 \\) in amber. Slide \\( x \\): the <em>height</em> of the amber curve equals the <em>slope</em> of the indigo one.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "canvasId": "apDerivCanvas",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · A function and its derivative",
          "ar": null
        },
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A cubic function and its derivative plotted on the same axes",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "apDerivDataBtn",
          "panelId": "apDerivDataPanel",
          "descId": "apDerivDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "apDerivDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled points on f(x) and its derivative f′(x)",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "x",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "f(x)",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "f′(x)",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "apDerivX",
            "label": {
              "en": "Point <b>x =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": -2.5,
            "max": 2.5,
            "value": 1,
            "step": 0.1,
            "valueDisplayId": "apDerivXV",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Point x",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "apDerivFx",
            "label": {
              "en": "f(x)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "—",
            "colorClass": "indigo"
          },
          {
            "id": "apDerivSlope",
            "label": {
              "en": "f '(x) = slope",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "—",
            "colorClass": "amber"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "Where \\( f \\) is flat (\\( f'=0 \\)) the amber curve crosses zero — those are the max and min of \\( f \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — The derivative",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\( f'(x)=\\displaystyle\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} \\). From it follow the power, constant-multiple, sum, product, and quotient rules.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Definition",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\lim_{h\\to0}\\dfrac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Power rule",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}x^{n}=nx^{n-1} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Product",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (uv)'=u'v+uv' \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Quotient",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\left(\\dfrac{u}{v}\\right)'=\\dfrac{u'v-uv'}{v^{2}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Differentiate \\( f(x)=3x^{4}-2x \\).</p>\\[ f'(x)=12x^{3}-2. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Differentiability from the limit definition",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find \\(f'(x)\\) for \\(f(x)=x^2-3x\\) using the limit definition.</p>\\[f'(x)=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{(x+h)^2-3(x+h)-(x^2-3x)}{h}=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{2xh+h^2-3h}{h}=\\lim_{h\\to0}(2x+h-3)=2x-3.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Differentiate \\(y=x^4\\sin x\\). (Product rule)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(y'=4x^3\\sin x+x^4\\cos x\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
